{"ts": "2026-11-10T19:22:24.575934Z", "run_id": "r-20261110T1839Z-5522", "unit": "openspec:add-tool-invocation", "seq": 74, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "Read the frozen test, the rule, the stub, the new red test, the unit spec, the credentials spec and task 1.1. The rule flags any non-inventoried value import of the gateway index; the spec mandates such an import in request.ts and a three-path inventory, so the two-path [] assertion at line 22 necessarily fails after green. The credentials spec explicitly provides that a later caller adds itself in a named task, and task 1.1 names the inventory edit. The suggested edit is the minimal consistent change and does not weaken the test, so the clarifier suggestion is right.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.4250184999999997, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "a4887cf72a6ccc0994f13ce393cf463d9e76a1969a0e83b12ca6354dfdd609e6", "checked": [{"ref": "src/credentials/egress-site.test.ts:22", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(checkEgressSites(readSnapshot(), [\"src/credentials/vault-call.ts\", \"src/main.ts\"]), []);", "claim": "The frozen test asserts no violations on the real snapshot with the two-path inventory."}, {"ref": "test/arch/egress-sites.ts:25", "quote": "if (resolveSpecifier(file.path, ref.specifier) !== GATEWAY_INDEX) continue;\n      importers.add(file.path);\n      if (allowed.includes(file.path)) continue;", "claim": "Any non-test src file that value-imports the gateway index and is not in the allowed list yields an ARCH_EGRESS_SITE violation."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-tool-invocation/specs/tool-invocation/spec.md:15", "quote": "This change SHALL add `src/runtimes/invoke/request.ts` to the frozen egress inventory, leaving it `[\"src/credentials/vault-call.ts\", \"src/main.ts\", \"src/runtimes/invoke/request.ts\"]`, and it SHALL be the only file of `src/runtimes/` that imports the gateway by value (`bodyDigest`).", "claim": "The spec requires request.ts to value-import the gateway, which makes the two-path [] assertion fail."}, {"ref": "openspec/specs/credentials/spec.md:77", "quote": "a later caller adds itself in a named task", "claim": "The credentials spec foresees a later unit growing the inventory in a named task."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-tool-invocation/tasks.md:5", "quote": "set the inventory of `test/arch/egress-sites.test.ts::C-76ead8ea the engine's egress sites are exactly the inventory` to the three paths of the inventory scenario", "claim": "Task 1.1 is the named task that grows the inventory to three paths."}, {"ref": "test/arch/egress-sites.test.ts:56", "quote": "checkEgressSites(readSnapshot(), [\n        \"src/credentials/vault-call.ts\",\n        \"src/main.ts\",\n        \"src/runtimes/invoke/request.ts\",\n      ]),", "claim": "The red step already asserts the three-path inventory in the arch test, which the credentials test must match."}, {"ref": "src/runtimes/invoke/request.test.ts:243", "quote": "test(\"C-2a04f1cb only request ts is an egress site of runtimes\", () => {", "claim": "A new test of this unit traces the inventory scenario, so the edit to the old test needs no new criterion trace of its own."}, {"ref": "src/runtimes/invoke/request.ts:1", "quote": "// Signature stub (milestone scaffold, docs/decisions/0002): the change that owns this file implements it.", "claim": "request.ts is still a stub with no gateway import, so the conflict appears only at green, as the implementer says."}]}
